<main class="page">
  <div class="content">
    <a href="/blog" class="back">← Back to Blog</a>
    
    <h1>Pulse v0.10.0: The Eval Exorcism</h1>
    <span class="date">January 24, 2025</span>
    
    <div class="body">
      <p class="lead">Pulse v0.10.0 marks a critical milestone in our framework's maturity. We have completely removed the usage of <code>eval()</code> from our runtime, addressing major security and performance concerns.</p>
      
      <h3>🛡️ Security & Performance</h3>
      <p>Previous versions relied on <code>eval()</code> to execute variable bindings in the DOM. This was unsafe and de-optimized by JS engines. v0.10.0 introduces a <strong>Secure Runtime</strong>:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>No Eval:</strong> Replaced with <code>new Function</code> constructors that are safer and optimizable.</li>
        <li><strong>Scope Isolation:</strong> Bindings can only access strictly defined scope variables, preventing global leakage.</li>
        <li><strong>Compilation Cache:</strong> Repeated expressions are cached for high-performance re-evaluation.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>📦 Build Optimization</h3>
      <p>We've enhanced the production build pipeline:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Aggressive Minification:</strong> Reduced bundle size by ~40%.</li>
        <li><strong>Tree Shaking:</strong> Unused primitives are automatically stripped from the final build.</li>
        <li><strong>Splitting:</strong> Better chunking for faster initial loads.</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>✨ v0.9 vs v10.0 Comparison</h3>
      <p>The Eval Exorcism brings massive improvements.</p>
      
      <div class="table-container">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Feature</th>
              <th>v0.9 (Legacy)</th>
              <th>v0.10 (Secure)</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Bindings</strong></td>
              <td><code>eval()</code> (Unsafe)</td>
              <td><code>safeEvaluate</code> (Secure)</td>
            </tr>
             <tr>
              <td><strong>Scope</strong></td>
              <td>Leaky (Globals accessible)</td>
              <td>Isolated (Strict Scope)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Bundle Strategy</strong></td>
              <td>Standard</td>
              <td>Minified & Tree-Shaken</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Bundle Size</strong></td>
              <td>1.2 MB (Dev)</td>
              <td>0.7 MB (Prod)</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</main>

